# ANDRADA.ONE ROUTING (Oct 2026) — one domain, one person, three names, each owning part of the work:
#   louis.andrada.one → Artworks (the home page)    han.andrada.one → Oeuvre    odi.andrada.one → Photography
#   andrada.one       → the Links page (the hub: every name, every door)
# Same site on every host (Netlify domain aliases). Netlify reads this file BEFORE the [[redirects]]
# in netlify.toml. First match wins, so an exact address comes before the /* that would also catch
# it. "!" = force (applies even though a file exists there). 200 = served in place: the address bar
# keeps the subdomain. 301 = moved for good (browsers and search engines remember it).
# The pages' own <link rel=canonical> says the same thing (_partials/canonical.html).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Front pages. louis.andrada.one/ is the home page itself, so it needs no rule.
https://andrada.one/            /links/index.html          200!
https://han.andrada.one/        /oeuvre/index.html         200!
https://odi.andrada.one/        /photography/index.html    200!

https://www.andrada.one/*       https://andrada.one/:splat   301!

# A section asked for on andrada.one itself moves to its face (one address per page).
https://andrada.one/artworks/                   https://louis.andrada.one/                          301!
https://andrada.one/artworks/*                  https://louis.andrada.one/artworks/:splat           301!
